<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is Logistics & Transport Payroll</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>Specialised wage processing for the <strong>layered logistics workforce</strong>: truck drivers (MTWA hours/overtime/trip allowance), <strong>warehouse shift workers</strong> (Factories Act, Bhiwandi 24/7), <strong>JNPT CHA/CFS staff</strong>, fleet owner payments (S.194C TDS), <strong>contract labour</strong> (loaders, hamalis, dock workers), and office/operations staff. Multi-location, multi-state compliance.</p><p><strong>MTWA 1961</strong>: max 8 hrs driving/day, 48 hrs/week, rest periods, overtime double wages. <strong>Fleet owner TDS</strong>: S.194C 1-2% on 50-500 attached vehicles - PAN verification + threshold tracking. <strong>Bhiwandi warehouses</strong>: 3 shifts, Factories Act overtime, seasonal surges 30-50%. <strong>Contract labour CLRA S.21</strong>: principal employer liable. <strong>Multi-state drivers</strong>: PF/ESI filed Mumbai, ESI Pehchan card across India. <strong>50-80% annual attrition</strong> for drivers and warehouse workers. <strong>Gig riders</strong>: SSC 2020 evolving.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Logistics Payroll in Mumbai:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>MTWA 1961:</strong> Motor Transport Workers Act. Max 8 hrs driving/day, 48/week. Rest: 30 min after 5 hrs; 9 hrs between duties. Overtime = double wages. Trip + night halt allowance.</p><p><strong>S.194C Fleet TDS:</strong> 1% individual/HUF, 2% company on goods carriage payments. Exemption: PAN + turnover &lt; Rs 1 Cr (Rs 10 Cr if 95%+ digital). 26Q quarterly + Form 16A.</p><p><strong>Bhiwandi Warehouse:</strong> Factories Act. 3 shifts 24/7. Overtime double rate &gt;9 hrs/day or &gt;48 hrs/week. Night allowance 10-20%. Factory inspector visits.</p><p><strong>CLRA S.21:</strong> Contract labour at ports/warehouses. Principal employer liable if contractor defaults. Form I registration for 20+ workers.</p><p><strong>Multi-State Drivers:</strong> PF/ESI filed with EPFO/ESIC Mumbai. ESI Pehchan card for cashless across states. Maharashtra PT for all.</p>

                </div>
            </div>
