                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What payroll compliance applies to logistics companies in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>MTWA 1961 (driver hours, overtime, rest), Factories Act (warehouse shifts), PF (20+, 12%+12%), ESI (10+, ≤ Rs 21,000), TDS S.192 (salary) + S.194C (fleet owners), Maharashtra PT, Payment of Wages/Gratuity/Bonus, CLRA 1970 (20+ contract workers). JNPT/port operations may have additional compliance.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Is PF and ESI mandatory for drivers and warehouse workers?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. PF for 20+ employees (all categories). ESI for 10+ employees, wages ≤ Rs 21,000 - covers most drivers, warehouse workers, loaders, helpers. Multi-state drivers: ESI Pehchan card for cashless across India. Even contract drivers on company rolls require PF/ESI. Remitted by 15th.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How much does logistics payroll cost in Mumbai?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Small transport: Rs 5,000-12,000/month. Mid-size trucking: Rs 12,000-30,000. Large transport: Rs 30,000-80,000. 3PL warehouse Bhiwandi: Rs 25,000-1,00,000. Freight forwarder/CHA: Rs 15,000-40,000. Courier: Rs 20,000-75,000. Large group: Rs 1,00,000-4,00,000. Fleet owner 194C add-on: Rs 5,000-25,000.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How is driver salary structured?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>MTWA structure: basic + DA + trip/outstation allowance (daily batta) + night halt + overtime at double wages (>8 hrs driving/day or >48 hrs/week). Variable trip components change monthly based on actual trips. Separate from office CTC. Long-haul vs local driver structures differ. Patron configures per MTWA.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Do fleet owners need TDS deducted on payments?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. S.194C: 1% individual/HUF, 2% company on goods carriage payments. Exemption: transporter provides PAN + turnover < Rs 1 Cr (Rs 10 Cr if 95%+ digital). 26Q quarterly + Form 16A annually. Patron manages PAN verification, threshold tracking, and complete 194C compliance.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How is multi-state driver payroll handled?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>PF/ESI filed with EPFO/ESIC Mumbai (establishment state). Drivers across 5-15 states covered under same code. ESI Pehchan card for cashless hospital access across India. Maharashtra PT applies to all employees regardless of where they work. Branch PT separately if in other states.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Quick Answers -->
            <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:32px;">
                <p><strong>Quick Answers</strong></p>
                <p><strong>Truck driver ka overtime kaise?</strong> MTWA: 8 ghante se zyada driving ya 48 ghante/hafta se zyada = double wages. Trip allowance outstation ke liye alag. Night halt allowance bhi milta hai.</p><p><strong>Fleet owner ko TDS katna zaroori?</strong> Haan - S.194C: 1% (individual) ya 2% (company). PAN + Rs 1 Cr se kam turnover pe exemption. 26Q quarterly file karna padta hai.</p><p><strong>Bhiwandi warehouse shift payroll?</strong> Factories Act: 3 shifts 24/7. 9 ghante se zyada pe double wages. Night allowance 10-20% extra. Leave 20 din pe 1 din.</p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

